orig":"12","parent":{"$ref":"#/pictures/0"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":515.6666666666666,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":163.66666666666669,"r":175.0,"t":525.0},"charspan":[0,2],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/30","text":"12"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"16","parent":{"$ref":"#/pictures/0"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":516.3333333333334,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":190.33333333333334,"r":201.66666666666666,"t":525.6666666666666},"charspan":[0,2],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/31","text":"16"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"Eb/No[dB]","parent":{"$ref":"#/pictures/0"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":500.33333333333337,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":124.33333333333333,"r":167.0,"t":511.0},"charspan":[0,9],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/32","text":"Eb/No[dB]"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"10-5","parent":{"$ref":"#/pictures/0"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":526.4713991181756,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":63.82631320676994,"r":80.84035345989673,"t":533.8619342151578},"charspan":[0,4],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/33","text":"10-5"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"requires a Eb / No of about 14 dB for the conventional correlation receiver, and a Eb / No of about 8 dB for the fourfinger RAKE receiver. In addition, a further simulation was done by combining the cluster 1 of the on-body channel and the IEEE802.15.3a CM1 channel [9] for simulating an additional indoor propagation characteristic. The BER degradation compared with the influence from the metal floor is only 1 dB at BER = 0.01. These results suggest that the high-speed transmission of 50 Mbps is possible in the onbody communication situation by the use of the RAKE receiver. Since the transmission speed of 10 Mbps may be enough when limiting it to the application of the healthcare and medical treatment, the influence of the multipath will be weakened and a further improvement of the BER performance can be expected.","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":291.0812417398573,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":49.094003740000005,"r":286.88931062000006,"t":463.67445580000003},"charspan":[0,824],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/34","text":"requires a Eb / No of about 14 dB for the conventional correlation receiver, and a Eb / No of about 8 dB for the fourfinger RAKE receiver. In addition, a further simulation was done by combining the cluster 1 of the on-body channel and the IEEE802.15.3a CM1 channel [9] for simulating an additional indoor propagation characteristic. The BER degradation compared with the influence from the metal floor is only 1 dB at BER = 0.01. These results suggest that the high-speed transmission of 50 Mbps is possible in the onbody communication situation by the use of the RAKE receiver. Since the transmission speed of 10 Mbps may be enough when limiting it to the application of the healthcare and medical treatment, the influence of the multipath will be weakened and a further improvement of the BER performance can be expected."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"section_header","level":1,"orig":"6. Conclusions","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":267.8131803888988,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":49.09400374000002,"r":118.00929298000008,"t":276.5230297600003},"charspan":[0,14],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/35","text":"6. Conclusions"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"This study aimed how to contain the environment reflection in a dynamic on-body UWB channel model. In addition to various human body postures, the reflection from the environment such as the floor was included. It has been shown that the environment reflection does not basically affect the multipath components in the first cluster that are generated by the diffraction and reflection of the human body. It is available to establish a body area channel model by a combination of the on-body model and the additional components from the environment. Using the impulse response expression of the channel model generated in such a way, the average BER performance of a typical IR-UWB system has been clarified. It has been found that the degradation at BER = 0.01 is 2-3 dB due to the influence of the reflected waves from the environment. A high-speed transmission of 50 Mbps on the body surface is possible by the use of the RAKE receiver structure.","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":209.24047525985725,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":49.09400374000002,"r":286.89429191999994,"t":252.98339848000035},"charspan":[0,228],"page_no":1},{"bbox":{"b":561.8612722198573,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":309.495,"r":547.3480899600003,"t":710.7853412000001},"charspan":[229,949],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/36","text":"This study aimed how to contain the environment reflection in a dynamic on-body UWB channel model. In addition to various human body postures, the reflection from the environment such as the floor was included. It has been shown that the environment reflection does not basically affect the multipath components in the first cluster that are generated by the diffraction and reflection of the human body. It is available to establish a body area channel model by a combination of the on-body model and the additional components from the environment. Using the impulse response expression of the channel model generated in such a way, the average BER performance of a typical IR-UWB system has been clarified. It has been found that the degradation at BER = 0.01 is 2-3 dB due to the influence of the reflected waves from the environment. A high-speed transmission of 50 Mbps on the body surface is possible by the use of the RAKE receiver structure."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"section_header","level":1,"orig":"References","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":541.0298906180258,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":309.495,"r":346.55596499999973,"t":547.9977876},"charspan":[0,10],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/37","text":"References"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","enumerated":true,"label":"list_item","marker":"[1]","orig":"[1] A.W. Astrin, H.-B. Li, and R. Kohno, 'Standardization for body area networks,' IEICE Trans. Commun., vol.E92-B, no.2, pp.366-372, Feb. 2009.","parent":{"$ref":"#/groups/0"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":499.5123729396137,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":311.83502136,"r":547.1801192099998,"t":526.28643819},"charspan":[0,144],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/38","text":"A.W. Astrin, H.-B. Li, and R. Kohno, 'Standardization for body area networks,' IEICE Trans. Commun., vol.E92-B, no.2, pp.366-372, Feb. 2009."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","enumerated":true,"label":"list_item","marker":"[2]","orig":"[2] A. Fort, J. Ryckaert, C. Desset, P. De Doncker, P. Wambacq, and L. Van Biesen, 'Ultra-wideband channel model for communication around the human body,' IEEE Trans. J. Sel. Areas Commun., vol.24, no.4, pp.927-933, April 2006.","parent":{"$ref":"#/groups/0"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":459.8531553396138,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":311.83502136,"r":547.2446770199991,"t":496.5268818},"charspan":[0,227],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/39","text":"A. Fort, J. Ryckaert, C. Desset, P. De Doncker, P. Wambacq, and L. Van Biesen, 'Ultra-wideband channel model for communication around the human body,' IEEE Trans. J. Sel. Areas Commun., vol.24, no.4, pp.927-933, April 2006."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","enumerated":true,"label":"list_item","marker":"[3]","orig":"[3] A. Taparugssanagorn, A. Rabbachin, M. Hamalainen, J. Saloranta, and J. Iinatti, 'A review of channel modeling for wireless body area network in wireless medical communications,' Proc. 11th Int. Symp. on Wireless Personal Multimedia Communications (WPMC'08), Lapland, Finland, FL3-1, Sept. 2008.","parent":{"$ref":"#/groups/0"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":410.2337037696139,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":311.83502136,"r":547.2263457900003,"t":456.8676642000001},"charspan":[0,298],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/40","text":"A. Taparugssanagorn, A. Rabbachin, M. Hamalainen, J. Saloranta, and J. Iinatti, 'A review of channel modeling for wireless body area network in wireless medical communications,' Proc. 11th Int. Symp. on Wireless Personal Multimedia Communications (WPMC'08), Lapland, Finland, FL3-1, Sept. 2008."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","enumerated":true,"label":"list_item","marker":"[4]","orig":"[4] H. Sawada, T. Aoyagi, J. Takada, K.Y. Yazdandoost, and R. Kohno, 'Channel model for wireless body area network,' Presented at Int. Symp. on Medical Information and Commun. Tech. (ISMICT), Yokohama, Japan, Dec. 2007.","parent":{"$ref":"#/groups/0"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":370.574486169614,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":311.83502136,"r":547.2191726999986,"t":407.2482126300002},"charspan":[0,219],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/41","text":"H. Sawada, T. Aoyagi, J. Takada, K.Y. Yazdandoost, and R. Kohno, 'Channel model for wireless body area network,' Presented at Int. Symp. on Medical Information and Commun. Tech. (ISMICT), Yokohama, Japan, Dec. 2007."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","enumerated":true,"label":"list_item","marker":"[5]","orig":"[5] Q. Wang, T. Tayamachi, I. Kimura, and J. Wang, 'An on-body channel model for UWB body area communications for various postures,' IEEE Trans. Antennas Propag., vol.57, no.4, pp.991-998, April 2009.","parent":{"$ref":"#/groups/0"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":340.81492977961403,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":311.83502136,"r":547.1745401399995,"t":367.58899503000026},"charspan":[0,200],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/42","text":"Q. Wang, T. Tayamachi, I. Kimura, and J. Wang, 'An on-body channel model for UWB body area communications for various postures,' IEEE Trans. Antennas Propag., vol.57, no.4, pp.991-998, April 2009."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","enumerated":true,"label":"list_item","marker":"[6]","orig":"[6] A.F. Molisch, 'Ultrawideband propagation channels - Theory, measurement, and modeling,' IEEE Trans. Veh. Technol., vol.54, no.5, pp.1528-1545, Sept. 2005.","parent":{"$ref":"#/groups/0"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":311.0553733896141,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":311.83502136,"r":547.2574291799992,"t":337.7688658800003},"charspan":[0,158],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/43","text":"A.F. Molisch, 'Ultrawideband propagation channels - Theory, measurement, and modeling,' IEEE Trans. Veh. Technol., vol.54, no.5, pp.1528-1545, Sept. 2005."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","enumerated":true,"label":"list_item","marker":"[7]","orig":"[7] A.F. Molisch, D. Cassioli, C.-C. Chong, S. Emami, A. Fort, B. Kannan, J. Karedal, J. Kunisch, H.G. Schantz, K. Siwiak, and M.Z. Win, 'A comprehensive standardized model for ultrawideband propagation channels,' IEEE Trans. Antennas Propag., vol.54, no.11, pp.3151-3166, Nov. 2006.","parent":{"$ref":"#/groups/0"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":261.4359218196141,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":311.83502136,"r":547.2630082499996,"t":308.00930949000036},"charspan":[0,283],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/44","text":"A.F. Molisch, D. Cassioli, C.-C. Chong, S. Emami, A. Fort, B. Kannan, J. Karedal, J. Kunisch, H.G. Schantz, K. Siwiak, and M.Z. Win, 'A comprehensive standardized model for ultrawideband propagation channels,' IEEE Trans. Antennas Propag., vol.54, no.11, pp.3151-3166, Nov. 2006."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","enumerated":true,"label":"list_item","marker":"[8]","orig":"[8] Q. Wang and J. Wang, 'Performance of ultra wideband on-body communication based on statistical channel model,' IEICE Trans. Commun., vol.E93-B, no.4, pp.833-841, April 2010.","parent":{"$ref":"#/groups/0"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":231.67636542961418,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":311.83502136,"r":547.2550381499995,"t":258.4504306800004},"charspan":[0,177],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/45","text":"Q. Wang and J. Wang, 'Performance of ultra wideband on-body communication based on statistical channel model,' IEICE Trans. Commun., vol.E93-B, no.4, pp.833-841, April 2010."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","enumerated":true,"label":"list_item","marker":"[9]","orig":"[9] J. Foerster, 'Path loss proposed text and S-V model information,' IEEE P802.15-02 / xxxr0-SG3a, pp.833-841, July 2007.","parent":{"$ref":"#/groups/0"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":211.71695232000047,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":311.83502136,"r":547.0932451200003,"t":228.69087429000047},"charspan":[0,122],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/46","text":"J. Foerster, 'Path loss proposed text and S-V model information,' IEEE P802.15-02 / xxxr0-SG3a, pp.833-841, July 2007."}],"version":"1.10.0"}